{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":605449,"num_turns":98,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"09806fd3-8b9e-430d-b8bc-3efc905d61fe","total_cost_usd":6.811012000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":136747,"cache_read_input_tokens":8588232,"output_tokens":45794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14910},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":136747,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1295,"cache_read_input_tokens":156543,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3731,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.003816,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":152,"outputTokens":45794,"cacheReadInputTokens":8588232,"cacheCreationInputTokens":136747,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":6.807196,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Work is complete and validated; the last gate (`go test ./...` across the whole repo) is still running. Summary so far:\n\n**Finding.** `internal/godriver/identity.go` canonicalized the running manager with `filepath.EvalSymlinks`, while every other canonicalization in the driver (`selectToolchain`, `verifySelectedRoot`, `mustPhysical`) uses `physicalPath`. On unix those are the same function, so the darwin/linux symlinked launch already canonicalized. On Windows they are not: a manager installed under a **directory junction** was refused with `worker_identity_invalid: cannot canonicalize the manager executable` before any substitution check ran — the operator's launch shape treated as a fault, which is the inversion `profiles/manager.md:213-216` orders against (\"resolves its own executable to a canonical regular installed file, rejects symlink, reparse-point, and hard-link substitution\"). `platform_windows.go:20-36` already documents this junction shape as real (the GH Actions Go tool cache is published that way).\n\n**Fix.** One line plus its rationale comment: `resolveExecutableIdentity` canonicalizes with `physicalPath(absolute)`. Unix behavior is bit-identical; on Windows every link kind resolves in one `GetFinalPathNameByHandle` call. The substitution battery downstream is untouched and now applies to the physical file.\n\n**Tests** (`identity_test.go`, `identity_windows_test.go`, probe mode in `main_test.go`): four launch shapes resolve to one identity; substitution through a link still fails closed (dangling, directory, empty, hard-linked, retargeted shim, mutated bytes); a real re-exec of the test binary through a shim link; the full `Build` manager→worker identity handshake with `managerExecutable` pointed at a link.\n\n**Evidence.** `os.Executable` reports the **link** path, not the target, on both darwin/arm64 and windows/amd64 — measured, so canonicalization is not a no-op there. Red→green on the native Windows host (`ssh win`, go1.25.5 windows/amd64): pre-fix baseline junction test exits **1** (expected red, this is the bug), post-fix full `go test ./internal/godriver/` exits **0** (248.8s).\n\n**Gates, real exit codes, run standalone:** darwin `go test ./internal/godriver/ -count=1` 0 · `go build ./...` 0 · `go vet ./...` 0 · `gofmt -l cmd internal` 0/empty · `golangci-lint run` 0 (\"0 issues\") · `GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/godriver/` 0. `GOOS=windows golangci-lint run` exits 1 with 10 findings, all in files this change does not touch (`buildcache/protection_windows.go`, `buildrepo/protection_windows.go`, `godriver/controls_windows.go`, `godriver/platform_windows.go`, `managerlock/identity_windows.go`+test); the native lint gate the repo uses is clean. Also note `go vet ./...` first failed on `internal/ui` because the fresh worktree hadn't initialized the `skill-go-testing-tools` submodule — fixed with `git submodule update --init --recursive`, unrelated.\n\nArtifacts attached to the board (write-up + both Windows logs), logbook entry written, changes live on `task/TASK-260822-27bvo4-symlink-launcher` in `.temp/TASK-260822-27bvo4/worktree` — uncommitted, per standing orders. One thing I deliberately left out of scope: `internal/managerlock/identity.go:63,84` also uses `filepath.EvalSymlinks`, but for the lock path rather than the executable — worth a separate look if the story wants that boundary covered.\n\nI'll run the board handoff once `go test ./...` reports.","ttft_ms":2070,"ttft_stream_ms":1230,"time_to_request_ms":41,"type":"result","duration_ms":965919,"uuid":"b00782ab-d173-4fa6-a69c-511402832dc1"}
